    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="39">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 39</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.b"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.21"/><pb n="515" ed="#liebermann"/>Ententivement se purpensent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.22"/> cil qui les jugementz unt a faire, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.1"/> si jugent, cum [il<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.23"/>] desirent, quant il dient: ‘Dimitte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.c"/> nobis debita nostra’.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.24"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="515" ed="#liebermann"/>De iudiciis et iudicibus. Diligentissime attendant iudices, ut ita iudicent proximum, sicut se a Deo paciscuntur iudicandos, cum dicunt: ‘Dimitte nobis debita nostra, sicut et nos dimittimus debitoribus nostris’<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.c-2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="39" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="270" ed="#robertson"/>Ententivement se purpensent cil qui les jugementz unt a faire, que si jugent cum [il] desirent quant il dient: "Dimitte nobis debita nostra."</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="515" ed="#liebermann"/>39. Aufmerksam mögen sich bedenken die, welche die Urtheile zu fällen haben, dass sie so urtheilen, wie sie wünschen, wenn sie sprechen: ‘Dimitte nobis debita nostra’.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">39. Let those who have to pronounce the judgements consider attentively that they judge as they wish when they say: ‘Dimitte nobis debita nostra’.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="271" ed="#robertson"/>Those who have to give judgments shall earnestly take heed that they judge as they themselves desire when they say: "Forgive us our trespasses."</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="515"><ref target="clause:IICn_2a">II Cn 2a</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">II Cn. 2a</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 270–271 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 515, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">515</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">der Schluss der</hi> Leis <hi rend="italic">folgt zumeist</hi> Cnut, <hi rend="italic">der aber auch schon oben benutzt ist. Aus Gleichheit der Form folgt Identität des Verfassers von Anfang bis Ende, trotz sachlicher Widersprüche gegen den Anfang</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the end of the Leis mostly follows Cnut, who, however, has already been used above as well. From the uniformity of form it follows that the author is the same from beginning to end, despite contradictions in substance with the beginning</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">515</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Matth.</hi> 6, 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Matth. 6, 12</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">515</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">515</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XLI. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XLI. I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">515</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">purpers. <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">purpers. Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">515</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Io;</hi> si <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in Io; si Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">515</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">kein Absatz I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">no paragraph break I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_39.lnote.oe.c-2" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">515</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgen</hi> 39, 1. 2. 40 <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">39, 1. 2. 40 follow in S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_39.lnote.de._" n="-" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">291</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Erklärungen zu 39ff. stehen zur Quelle, Cnut</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Notes on 39ff. are given under the source, Cnut</seg></note>
      </div>
